    "title": "Retirement Party Sunday For Longtime GMC Employee Connie Osborn - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Evan Ellis ,\n8 hours ago Gritman Medical Center will celebrate the retirement of Chief Quality Officer Connie Osborn following 50 years of service to the Moscow hospital. Osborn joined Gritman as a nurse’s aide in 1976 while attending nursing school. During her career, she spent 17 years in the Critical Care Unit, served as director of the Medical-Surgical Unit, established Gritman’s Cardiac Rehabilitation program and oversaw the hospital’s rural clinics. She became Chief Quality Officer in 2006. Read full article",
